    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="192" ed="#liebermann"/>Eac we cwædon, gyf him hundred bedrife tród on oðer hundred, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mon cyðe ðam hundredesm<hi rend="italic">en<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.16"/></hi>, ⁊ he ðonne ðær midfare.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="192" ed="#liebermann"/>Etiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.7"/> (Amplius) diximus, si hundredum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.2"/> minet uestigium in aliud hundredum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.2"/>, ut notificetur hominibus illius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.27"/> (ipsius) hundredi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.6"/>, et ipsi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.7"/> (idem) cum eo uadant.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="193" ed="#liebermann"/>Item diximus, quod, si persone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.13"/> unius centenarii sequantur uestigia (furati<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.14"/> animalis) in territorium alterius centenarii, nuncietur concionatori (illius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.12"/> scilicet, quo iam peruenerunt), qui simul cum (illis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Hu_5.lnote.oe.15"/>) proficiscatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="18" ed="#robertson"/>Eac we cwædon, gyf him hundred bedrife tród on oðer hundred, þæt mon cyðe ðam hundredesmen<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Hu_5.robnote.fn.1"/>, ⁊ he ðonne ðær midfare.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="193" ed="#liebermann"/>Auch bestimmten wir: wenn ihm [dem Nachspürer verlorener Fahrniss] eine Hundertschaft die Spur in eine andere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Hu_5.lnote.de.1"/> Hundertschaft leitet, dass man [es] dem Vorsteher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_5.lnote.de.2"/> letzterer Hundertschaft melde, und der dann da mitziehe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_5.lnote.de.3"/> [auf Nachspürung].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">We also determined: if a hundred leads the track for him [the man tracing lost property] into another hundred, that it be reported to the head of the latter hundred, and that he then go along there [in the search].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="19" ed="#robertson"/>We have further declared, that if one hundred follow up a track into another hundred, notice shall be given to the chief official of the latter<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Hu_5.robnote.n.1"/>, and he shall then take part in the search.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="433" ed="#whitelock"/>Further, we decreed, if one hundred follows up a trail into another hundred, that is to be made known to the man in charge of that hundred, and he is then to go with them.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">m̄, <hi rend="italic">darüber im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> anna.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">m̄, above it anna. in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Glosse</hi>) <hi rend="italic">aus Hk; fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(gloss) from Hk; lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Glosse</hi>) <hi rend="italic">aus Hr; fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(gloss) from Hr; lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> illo <hi rend="italic">Hk; fehlt</hi> [<hi rend="italic">ursprünglicher?</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from illo Hk; lacking [more original?] in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond;</hi> (<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>) <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">before the bracket Lond; (bracketed) the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-etum <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-etum RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ipsius <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ipsius RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-eti <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-eti RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Hundred 13. 15</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Hundred 13. 15</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q irrt wie <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 2⁴. 4²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q errs as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 2⁴. 4²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_5.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Begleitung der Spurfolge durch den Gutsherrn oder den Magistrat fordern die Stellen Spurfolge 6. b mit Fränkischer Parallele</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The passages Spurfolge 6. b, with a Frankish parallel, require that the following of the trail be accompanied by the lord of the manor or the magistrate</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Hu_5.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The <hi rend="italic">hundredesman</hi> (called <hi rend="italic">hundredes ealdor</hi> in IV Edg. 8, 1) performs the duty ascribed to the reeve in VI As. 8, 4.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Hu_5.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">18</biblScope></bibl><label>hundredesmen</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">m̃</hi> with <hi rend="italic">anna</hi> added above in later handwriting; <hi rend="italic">men</hi> Lieb.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
